WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:03.051
(crowd cheering)

00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:11.276
(crowd cheering)

00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:16.788
Now

00:00:18.593 --> 00:00:21.343
(crowd cheering)

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.233
It is

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.780
clearly so exciting for people to see

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.643
the two of us together.

00:00:29.643 --> 00:00:32.620
(laughter)

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.010
I have a confession to make,

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.330
which is we didn't really meet,

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.350
but we met in a way a couple of years ago.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.630
But you probably won't remember.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.463
No

00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:41.409
And I'll excuse you.

00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:42.550
Okay.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.150
Most people think I'm Ralph
Malph from Happy Days.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.980
Hi! How are ya? Huh, Richie!

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.120
Uh, I was in Washington, D. C.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.700
about two and a half
years ago doing an event.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.050
I got back from the event late at night.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.520
They put me up at this nice hotel.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.980
I walk through the
lobby. I'm really tired.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.820
I get on the elevator. The
elevator door starts to close.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:05.653
And you know, you're really tired.

00:01:05.653 --> 00:01:07.297
The elevator door's closing
and someone shouted out

00:01:07.297 --> 00:01:09.880
"Hold the door! Hold the elevator!"

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.310
And I went to hit the button

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:14.110
and then thought, "It's, ugh."

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.090
It was, like, too much to
lean over to hit the button.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.150
I's like, "Eh." And I just lean back

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.010
and I don't hit the button.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.340
And as the door's closing, I see your face

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.370
in the closing door,
looking angrily at me.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.256
And the...

00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:29.340
(laughter)

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.893
and the door shut, and I was like,

00:01:31.893 --> 00:01:33.242
"Aaaaaahhh!"

00:01:33.242 --> 00:01:35.492
(laughter)

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:37.802
Goodnight.

00:01:37.802 --> 00:01:40.420
No. No! No, please!

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:41.800
Please!

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.410
Please stay! I didn't
realize. I was tired.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:46.243
Let me,

00:01:46.243 --> 00:01:47.492
I was tired, too.

00:01:47.492 --> 00:01:49.292
(laughter)

00:01:49.292 --> 00:01:50.392
No! No.

00:01:50.392 --> 00:01:52.360
Now, maybe you had a big
day. I had a big day, too.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.323
I'm sorry!

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.820
It's big of me to relive
this moment, I think.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.420
I could've just forgotten it,

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.450
but I felt I should
bring it up. And in fact,

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.799
I went up the stairs.

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:03.850
(laughter)

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.072
Seventeen floors.

00:02:05.072 --> 00:02:06.860
I heard someone...

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:07.762
I tried to find you.

00:02:07.762 --> 00:02:08.990
(laughter)

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:10.810
I heard someone banging on my door

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:11.670
about half an hour later.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.830
I didn't really recognize you,

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.232
but I was looking for the big, mean guy.

00:02:16.232 --> 00:02:17.573
(laughter)

00:02:17.573 --> 00:02:18.420
I'm so sorry!

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.253
I'm glad I found you.

00:02:19.253 --> 00:02:21.610
Yeah. Oh no. Let's straighten
this out, first of all.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.060
I want people to relive the horror

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.830
of what that was like for me.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.400
And we can recreate this right now.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.780
If you'd be so good, Harrison, to look

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.430
into that camera right now.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.393
You're tired.

00:02:30.393 --> 00:02:32.310
(laughter)

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.012
You're angry. You're...

00:02:34.012 --> 00:02:36.582
(laughter)

00:02:36.582 --> 00:02:38.665
You're tired and angry. And then,

00:02:38.665 --> 00:02:39.850
(laughter)

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.073
You make eye con-. Oh!

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:46.038
(applause)

00:02:49.054 --> 00:02:51.804
(crowd cheering)

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.240
Now, it's only fair to recreate

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.563
what it must have been
like for you to see this.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.130
(laughter)

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.430
I mean, you're the kind
of. You have so much clout,

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.093
you could easily have me killed.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.181
No, no, no.

00:03:18.181 --> 00:03:19.090
(laughter)

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:19.923
It's all in the works right now.

00:03:19.923 --> 00:03:21.220
No, no, no, no.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.131
Well, we're very happy that you're here.

00:03:23.131 --> 00:03:23.964
Well, thank you.

00:03:23.964 --> 00:03:26.252
Congratulations. The,
the number one movie.

00:03:26.252 --> 00:03:27.085
It's a cool thing.

00:03:27.085 --> 00:03:27.918
For the moment.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.413
You know something I don't.

00:03:30.413 --> 00:03:33.940
No, no, no. I'm very pleased,
the response has been great.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.860
Yeah. It's interesting, 'cause for you.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.310
I mean, you're famous for
being very cool-headed.

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.711
You know? You are, I think.

00:03:41.711 --> 00:03:44.750
You're a very cool guy.
You don't get excited.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.050
If I was in the number one movie,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.550
I'd be stirring the pot
dancing, wearing a thong.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:51.093
I'd be jumping around.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.650
I'd be very excited, to say the least.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.440
What excites you? I mean, if being in

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.870
the number one movie doesn't do it,

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:02.063
what really makes Harrison Ford wig out?

00:04:03.001 --> 00:04:04.610
(laughter)

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.443
Um.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:10.250
I guess I don't wig out. You know?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.950
Even if the following things happen?

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.890
What if you were to. We have
a few demonstrations, here.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.380
Would you get excited if you got to play

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.031
bass with Limp Bizkit?
Would this excite you?

00:04:19.031 --> 00:04:21.922
(laughter)

00:04:21.922 --> 00:04:23.172
Would that get you going?

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:24.903
Uh, um.

00:04:24.903 --> 00:04:27.140
What if, uh, you got to go streaking?

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.740
Would that really get you going?

00:04:30.043 --> 00:04:32.793
(crowd cheering)

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.750
What if we gave you a chance
to actually be reborn?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.140
What if you could be reborn?

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:41.881
Wouldn't that get you excited, right now?

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:44.131
(laughter)

00:04:45.378 --> 00:04:48.397
Look! You're wigging out!

00:04:48.397 --> 00:04:49.529
Yeah!

00:04:49.529 --> 00:04:52.138
(laughter)

00:04:52.138 --> 00:04:54.388
(applause)

00:05:00.248 --> 00:05:02.376
And I am wearing a thong!

00:05:02.376 --> 00:05:03.675
(laughter)

00:05:03.675 --> 00:05:04.508
Okay.

00:05:04.508 --> 00:05:05.630
Come on.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.880
(laughter)

00:05:09.673 --> 00:05:10.720
I didn't need to know that!

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.553
Oh, no, no. You should.

00:05:11.553 --> 00:05:13.030
That's why I didn't let
you on the elevator.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:15.690
All right now, let's talk about the film

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.510
What Lies Beneath. Scary movie.

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:21.980
Uh, yeah. Very, uh. I
think it's a thriller.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:26.590
It's a psychological scary,
rather than slasher scary.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.423
Right.

00:05:27.423 --> 00:05:28.256
Which is the usual form.

00:05:28.256 --> 00:05:29.470
Which can actually be
scarier, a lot of times.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.573
I think so, yeah.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.830
What's? I mean, do you like
scary movies in general?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.270
Is that something you enjoy?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.103
Uh, no.

00:05:36.103 --> 00:05:36.936
You don't really like them?

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:40.100
No, I'm glad there are
people that like 'em.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.458
But I don't.

00:05:41.458 --> 00:05:42.291
Yeah!

00:05:42.291 --> 00:05:43.124
(laughter)

00:05:43.124 --> 00:05:44.930
I don't really go to scary movies.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.380
What was the scariest movie you ever saw?

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.213
Bambi.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.317
(laughter)

00:05:48.317 --> 00:05:49.530
Bambi? Really?

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.363
Did you see it?

00:05:50.363 --> 00:05:52.450
Yes, I did. I saw Bambi a long time ago.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.228
Well, maybe you saw a
different version than I saw.

00:05:54.228 --> 00:05:55.061
(laughter)

00:05:55.061 --> 00:05:56.500
You saw this really scary version.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.580
No, I really saw the French version.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.120
It's really more scary.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.130
And it was very scary.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.440
No, it's scary. I mean,
the loss of a mother.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:04.540
That sort of thing is scary.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:05.980
Right, psychologically scary.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:06.813
Yeah, heartaches.

00:06:06.813 --> 00:06:08.790
Do you get scared a lot,
and do you scary easily?

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:09.660
Would you think?

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:10.493
No.

00:06:11.778 --> 00:06:13.298
(hissing)

00:06:13.298 --> 00:06:15.021
(laughter)

00:06:15.021 --> 00:06:16.247
You see what I mean?

00:06:16.247 --> 00:06:17.870
(laughter)

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.303
I so committed to this!

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.083
You did.

00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:22.360
Yeah, that's my charm.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.193
That's, uh.

00:06:23.193 --> 00:06:24.290
Can we say that's my charm?

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.678
It's a comedy rule.

00:06:25.678 --> 00:06:26.580
(laughter)

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.670
Commit!

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:29.190
I heard that you're thinking of doing

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.830
another Indiana Jones movie. Is that true?

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:32.663
Um, well not...

00:06:32.663 --> 00:06:34.879
(cheering)

00:06:37.147 --> 00:06:38.564
Nah, it's good.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.340
Yeah, I'm gonna do it alone in my backyard

00:06:46.191 --> 00:06:49.133
in Wyoming on video. I'm gonna do it.

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:50.060
Be everything, yeah.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:51.200
It's gonna be great, though.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.380
No. I would love to do one.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:56.060
We're waiting to have a script.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:56.893
Right.

00:06:56.893 --> 00:07:00.010
And a time for, uh, Spielberg

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:01.900
and Lucas and I to get together.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.950
Yeah, people will never
get tired of that genre.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.840
You could do it for, I mean. You could,

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.160
when you're eighty, you could do ones

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.200
where they just bring the
treasures to you and you're

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.054
(laughter)

00:07:13.054 --> 00:07:14.554
That's good! Yeah!

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:16.972
Good job!

00:07:16.972 --> 00:07:19.240
(laughter)

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.360
Just something to think about.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.749
Indiana Jones and the Comfortable Bed!

00:07:23.749 --> 00:07:25.181
(laughter)

00:07:25.181 --> 00:07:26.431
Nyeeeaargh! Oh!

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.423
Put that with the rest of them over there!

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.233
Um.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:34.975
Uh.

00:07:34.975 --> 00:07:35.890
(laughter)

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.180
Now, before you go, I have to ask you.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.060
You're, of course, probably one of

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.540
the biggest stars we
ever had on this show.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.267
Although, Mr. T's coming up tomorrow.

00:07:43.267 --> 00:07:44.838
(laughter)

00:07:44.838 --> 00:07:46.438
Uh, so don't get a swelled head.

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:49.380
Now, a lot of times big stars,

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.720
they have to leave right away.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.130
And I'm wondering, is there any
way we could get you to stay

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:55.660
until the very end of the
show at 1:30 for the credits.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.210
'Cause that would look so cool.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.347
1:30?

00:07:59.347 --> 00:08:01.150
(laughter)

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.926
You don't think so, huh?

00:08:02.926 --> 00:08:03.759
Uh-uh

00:08:03.759 --> 00:08:04.689
You're a busy guy, you can't do it.

00:08:04.689 --> 00:08:07.290
I would love to stay. I really would.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.123
Yeah.

00:08:08.123 --> 00:08:08.956
But, um.

00:08:10.288 --> 00:08:12.936
I have some cookies in the oven

00:08:12.936 --> 00:08:14.716
(laughter)

00:08:14.716 --> 00:08:17.331
That's the lamest thing
anyone's ever said to me!

00:08:17.331 --> 00:08:18.172
Oh yeah.

00:08:18.172 --> 00:08:19.005
But what if we did this.

00:08:19.005 --> 00:08:21.380
What if we shot the
ending of the show now,

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:23.880
and we throw it in there.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:27.350
And then, that way, we can
throw it at the end of the show.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.320
And then, people watching
the show will think

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.640
that you stayed 'til the end of the show.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.920
How's that sound?

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.059
No.

00:08:33.059 --> 00:08:34.380
(laughter)

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.670
Uh, folks, thanks for sticking all the way

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:37.503
to the end of the show.

00:08:37.503 --> 00:08:39.830
I can't believe Caroline Rhea
had to run and you stayed.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.736
Hit it Max! Goodnight, everybody!

00:08:41.736 --> 00:08:43.577
(upbeat music)

00:08:43.577 --> 00:08:45.827
(cheering)

